<misterromdescription>
    <!--
      Sega Model 2 core for MiSTer FPGA. Copyright (C) 2026 alphanu1
      SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

      P1.5 STEP 5, THE ORACLE. There is no CPU in this slice, so nothing writes
      the tilemap and the screen is black however good the fetcher is. This loads
      a CAPTURED tilemap state instead, dumped out of MAME at a known frame, so
      the 2D path can be compared against a reference picture rather than hoped
      at.

      m2tiles.bin is ROM-DERIVED. It is not in this repository and never will be.
      Regenerate it with tools/mame_m2_tiledump.lua; see docs/rom-layout.md.

      Layout, which the core's tilemap wiring must match:

        0x000000 +0x10000   tile RAM   (from i960 0x01000000)
        0x010000 +0x04000   palette    (from i960 0x01800000)
        0x014000 +0x80000   char RAM   (from i960 0x01080000)
        0x094000 +0x0c000   colorxlat  (from i960 0x01810000)

      Total 0xA0000, 640 KB, comfortably inside the 64 MB this SDRAM controller
      addresses, unlike the full 43.62 MB game set.

      THE COLORXLAT SECTION IS NEW and an image built before it will not have it.
      Model 2's palette runs each 5-bit channel through that table before a gamma
      curve rather than expanding it directly, and without it every fill colour
      in every game is a few units out - study R27, found by comparing a rendered
      frame against MAME pixel by pixel. The core sanity checks the section
      (entry 0 must map to 0 and entry 31 to 255 on all three channels) and falls
      back to the old expansion if it is absent or wrong, so an older image still
      renders exactly as it did.

      NOTE: an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen. Using one as a dash
      here produced a file that did not parse, and it was committed before being
      checked.
    -->
    <name>Model 2 2D Tilemap Test</name>
    <setname>m2tiles</setname>
    <rbf>Model2</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <year>1993</year>
    <manufacturer>Sega</manufacturer>
    <category>Test</category>

    <rom index="0" zip="m2tiles.zip" md5="none">
        <part name="m2tiles.bin"/>
    </rom>
</misterromdescription>
